---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '14 May 2026';
const effectiveDate = '14 May 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies Policy | Tenderpreneur"
  description="Which cookies and similar technologies Tenderpreneur uses, what they do, and how you can control them under POPIA."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-200 pb-8">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Cookies Policy</h1>
      <dl class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-900">Effective:</dt> <dd class="inline">{effectiveDate}</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-900">Last updated:</dt> <dd class="inline">{lastUpdated}</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:font-semibold prose-a:text-slate-900 prose-a:underline prose-a:decoration-slate-400 prose-a:underline-offset-2">
      <p class="lead">
        This policy explains what cookies and similar technologies we use, why
        we use them, and how you can control them. It supplements our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and forms part of it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-cookies-are">1. What cookies are</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files placed on your device by websites you
        visit. They allow the site to remember things like your login state or
        your cookie preferences. We also use similar technologies such as
        localStorage entries — wherever this policy says "cookie", treat it as
        including these.
      </p>

      <h2 id="lawful-basis">2. Lawful basis</h2>
      <p>
        Strictly necessary cookies are placed on the basis of our legitimate
        interest in providing a working service (POPIA s.11(1)(f)). All other
        cookies — analytics and marketing — are placed only with your prior
        consent (POPIA s.11(1)(a)). Non-essential cookies are off by default,
        and you can change your choice at any time.
      </p>

      <h2 id="control">3. How to control cookies</h2>
      <p>You have three independent controls:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Our consent banner.</strong> Click the button below to reopen it:
          <br>
          <button
            type="button"
            data-testid="open-cookie-settings"
            class="not-prose mt-3 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-slate-900 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm no-underline hover:bg-slate-800 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-slate-900 focus-visible:ring-offset-2"
            onclick="if (window.tpConsent) { window.tpConsent.open(); }"
          >
            Open cookie settings
          </button>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Your browser settings.</strong> Most browsers let you block or delete cookies. Blocking strictly necessary cookies will break the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Do Not Track / Global Privacy Control.</strong> If your browser sends a GPC signal we treat it as a withdrawal of consent for analytics and marketing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="categories">4. Cookies we use</h2>

      <h3 id="necessary">4.1 Strictly necessary (always on)</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>tp.consent.v1</code></td><td>Stores your cookie preferences so we don't keep asking.</td><td>12 months</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tp.session</code></td><td>Keeps you logged in during a browsing session.</td><td>Session</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tp.csrf</code></td><td>Anti-CSRF token, protects form submissions.</td><td>Session</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>__cf_bm</code></td><td>Cloudflare bot management — distinguishes humans from automated traffic.</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3 id="analytics">4.2 Analytics (consent required)</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>plausible_*</code></td><td>Aggregate page-view counts. No cross-site tracking, no personal identifiers.</td><td>24 hours</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        If we add a different analytics provider in future we will update this
        table and ask for fresh consent where the new processing is not
        equivalent.
      </p>

      <h3 id="marketing">4.3 Marketing (consent required)</h3>
      <p>
        We do not currently use marketing cookies. If we add any, they will be
        listed here and only set after you have given consent through the
        banner.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">5. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy when we add or remove cookies. The "Last
        updated" date at the top reflects the latest revision.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">6. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about cookies should go to
        <a href="mailto:privacy@tenderpreneur.co.za">privacy@tenderpreneur.co.za</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
